Decoded route data cache in core-legacy's RoutingContext.

unloadAllData() runs before every HH detailed segment and every start/end
search (it resets the search state, which lives in the RouteSegment
wrappers of loaded tiles) and threw away the decoded RouteDataObjects too, so
the same OBF blocks were decoded again: about 1,100 times for one 15 km
route, and again for every request. Decoding is CPU, not I/O (the same
times with the map in RAM). A process-wide cache keyed by (routing index,
block) now keeps the decoded objects (48 MB cap, cleared when full); each
load still runs acceptLine() and the exclusions and builds fresh
RouteSegments. Not used with conditional tags, direction points or
geocoding contexts, which change the objects.

Bench (route_bench, hh + 2 alternatives, identical results): 15 km
5.2 s -> 4.0 s first request, 3.4 s repeated; 25 km 7.3 -> 5.5 / 4.8 s.

Apply from the OsmAnd source-aggregate root after qnx-legacy-routing.patch.

